WEBVTT

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:04.070
Because everybody likes this planet

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.860
What's wrong, Survive?

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.660
Something has entered my sensing range.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.190
It's the gravity storm!

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.080
Gravity storm?

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.840
So this is a gravity storm...

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:37.100
So the gravity storm is the cause of the tectonic changes, both now and a thousand years ago?

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.260
The same as a thousand years ago...

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.240
What do we do? If that thing hits us, it's all over!

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.230
We don't know for sure that it will hit us!

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.460
Survive, can you compute the course of the gravity storm?

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:52.730
I shall try.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.390
The gravity storm will reach this planet in three days.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.410
Three days?

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:29.940
We can't stay here! Let's hurry and escape in the space ship!

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:31.810
Wait!

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.210
We can't do that!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.510
Abandoning this planet to save just ourselves...

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.900
What are you saying? In three days the gravity storm will hit us!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.910
But we still have three days!

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.850
Anyways, the first thing we should do is think of any way we might be able to destroy the gravity storm.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.060
We'll still have time to escape after that.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:53.150
Luna...

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.510
But I wonder if there is such a way.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.030
Maybe with the gravity control unit...

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.430
The gravity control unit?

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.940
Come look at this.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:17.440
The gravity control unit creates a new gravitational field...

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.600
...amplifying or suppressing the surrounding gravitational field.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:24.660
And we've seen that the gravity storm has an unstable gravitational field.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.450
Yeah! If we can analyze that instability...

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:32.630
...we can use the gravity control unit to generate an inverse gravitational field.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.360
Which means we should be able to destroy the gravity storm!

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:41.300
Luna...

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.340
Isn't that just an impractical theory?

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.330
That's impossible!

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:50.810
The problem is whether we can analyze the instability in the gravity storm in real-time.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:56.940
If we can just figure that out, we can link it to the computer and run a simulation...

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.440
I will analyze the instability.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.330
Can you do it, Survive?

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:06.580
It has taken me a thousand years to revitalize the ecosystem of this planet.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.160
I cannot allow it to be lost so easily.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.190
Then we're counting on you.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:14.040
Then we'd better get the simulation ready!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.410
Do what you want!

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.940
Data input all ready!

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.600
97.9% synchronized.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.100
Conversion system finished.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.730
With that, our preparations are done.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:41.820
Survive! How're things on your end?

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:45.820
I have just finished the analysis.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.120
So this is the instability of the gravitational field.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:57.280
Now we just use the gravity control unit to make the inverse field to this.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.110
There's little time. Start it up right away.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:09.650
You're right.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:10.960
Yes...

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.290
Inverting output of exotic controller.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.730
Quark-Gluon controller in operation.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.710
Tensor eigenvalue, check!

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.000
Is that really possible?

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:22.590
It's okay. I'm sure it'll work out.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.750
Alright! We should be able to generate the inverse field!

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.360
Then let's try it.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:29.900
Begin simulation!

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.840
The gravity storm is disappearing.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.190
Really?

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.130
Luna!

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:42.710
Yes...

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:51.950
It disappeared!

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.600
You did it, Chako!

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.230
Exactly accordin' to plan!

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.810
It disappeared! It disappeared!

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:04.330
Based on the data from this simulation, with the power from this space ship's gravity control unit...

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:08.040
...it seems that we can definitely destroy the gravity storm.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:09.460
So in that case...

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.310
...we have to get the space ship as close as possible...

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:16.030
...and release the gravity control unit into the gravity storm.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.380
Release it?

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:19.060
Hold on a second!

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:21.130
Then what will happen to us?

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:26.470
If we use the recoil from the release, we can fall back into the orbit of this planet.

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:29.790
No, I'm talking about the colony!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.840
If we release the gravity control unit, the space ship won't run any more.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.310
We won't be able to get back to the colony for the rest of our lives!

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.980
Survive, is there any other space ship?

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:41.980
No.

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.550
Nor is there any other gravity control unit with sufficient output.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:56.080
It looks like we'll just have to give up on going back to the colony.

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:57.840
What?

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.590
If the gravity storm hits it, this planet will collapse.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.160
We can't just abandon it.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.360
I disagree!

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:05.300
Howard!

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:10.390
But think about it! Why do we have to be sacrificed for the sake of this planet?

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:14.080
I'm going home! I'm definitely going home to the colony!

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.480
I agree with Howard.

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:17.430
Menori!

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.780
I understand your desire to save the planet.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:23.110
But what have we lived for all this time?

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:25.590
Wasn't it so we could go home to the colony?

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.580
That may be true...

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.560
I agree with Luna.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:30.610
You?

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:36.310
Of course I want to go home to the colony, but we're not the only ones on this planet.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:38.380
Pague!

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:44.410
Yes, and also the tobihanes, giant lizards, and various other plants and animals.

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:47.450
They're all alive, just like us!

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:52.260
I won't consider sacrificing them all just so we can go back to the colony!

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.110
Bell...

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:57.390
You want to protect this planet for the giant lizards?

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:00.160
It's not particularly for the giant lizards.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.510
I just...

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:02.940
It's just like Bell says!

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.240
It's not like we're in any hurry to go home now.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:11.240
As long as we keep transmitting the distress signal, help will come eventually.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:16.240
When you say,"go home," I ain't even sure which I'd rather you meant.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.760
Anyways, I'm against it!

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.650
No matter what anyone says, I'm going back to the colony!

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.310
I'm definitely using the space ship to go home!

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:26.150
Where are you going?

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:27.840
To gather food.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:31.850
We don't know how long it will take to get home to the colony, after all.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:33.460
Howard!

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:35.680
Luna...

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.730
I understand what Howard's saying.

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.630
I mean, the colony is Howard's birthplace, isn't it?

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:45.610
Adam...

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:49.890
I'll be right back!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.950
In any event, it's not a question that we need to answer right away.

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:57.370
We need time to think about it.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:09:59.790
Kaoru?

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:05.750
I'm going to check up on the space ship. Whether we save the planet or abandon it, we'll need it.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:08.490
I'll come too!

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:09.610
Me too!

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:11.380
W-wait for me!

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:22.660
Who'd do that for this planet? You must be kidding me!

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:25.780
Wait up, Howard! Wait!

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:35.710
Nothin' wrong.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.750
If we save this planet, we can't go back to the colony.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:42.010
If we go back to the colony, we can't save this planet.

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:44.080
What should we do?

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.540
It's a real complicated problem.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:51.550
Everyone! The Gyrostabilizer is completely perfect!

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:54.160
Yeesh, he's sure takin' it easy.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.480
Yes!

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:02.260
Is it really okay if we can't go back to the colony?

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:03.010
Yeah.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:06.950
My dad worked on planetary settlement.

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:11.830
Ever since I was little, I went from place to place with my dad.

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:16.930
The settlement was successful on some of those planets, and plants started to grow.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.210
But people had to stay in domes.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:23.560
Whatever the other differences were, they were all in domes.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.830
I always thought there was something strange about that.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.050
That was just fenced-in nature.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:34.060
But here we have real, living nature.

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:37.330
I don't want to destroy a planet like that.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:38.940
Bell...

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:42.350
Launch the space ship immediately?

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:45.730
The gravity storm is approaching. There is no time.

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:48.540
I know! But we can't do that.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.200
Please, wait a little while.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:56.000
Everyone's been faced with a grave decision. They're just confused.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:12:00.280
But they'll understand! Nobody's going to abandon this planet!

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:01.510
How do you know that?

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:04.250
Because everybody likes this planet.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.280
Likes this planet?

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:08.560
Please, wait just a little bit longer!

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:16.060
I cannot take off without your help.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:18.690
Very well. I shall wait.

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:20.530
Thank you, Survive!

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:22.780
Luna!

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:27.310
Hang on tight!

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:28.480
I know!

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:12.280
It's stopped.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.260
It seems to've settled down.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:28.700
Huh? Where's Tako?

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:31.740
Yeah, Tako? Where are you, Tako?

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:33.880
Over here!

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:34.660
Yikes!

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:38.260
How'd you end up all the way over there?

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:41.840
My head is so heavy that I can't get up!

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:51.310
Howard, hang on!

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:54.880
I'm gonna fall, I'm gonna fall, I'm gonna fall!

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:58.610
Don't let go! Don't you dare let go! I'm begging you...

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:12.280
I'm saved! Thanks!

00:14:12.690 --> 00:14:13.700
Howard...

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:16.290
Would you mind moving away?

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:21.880
Howard!

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.580
Are you okay?

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:26.940
Somehow, thank you.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.310
More importantly, what do we do?

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.830
What do we do...

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.600
I guess we wait for help to come.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:39.760
But...

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.540
Let's head that way.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:48.050
Even if we wait for help, it's possible they won't realize we're here...

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:51.730
...and if another earthquake comes and we fall off, that'll be the end.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:58.480
Howard!

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.100
I'm fine.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:06.730
If we go that way, there might be a place where we can climb to the top.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.460
Wait for me!

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:18.390
If you keep going so fast, I won't know if you fall off.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.780
Are you okay? You be careful too, Howard.

00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:38.830
Hey! I said you're too fast!

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:46.100
It's started raining.

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.430
Hang on tight!

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:00.580
Thank you.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:03.690
That's why I said not to go so fast.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:11.410
There doesn't seem to be any damage.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:16.550
Kaoru!

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.580
How are things there?

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:21.280
Looks like no problems over here.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:25.100
No problems! No problems! None, none, none!

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:44.410
Yeesh! How far do we have to go?

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:48.990
What's wrong?

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.160
Look over there! It's a Pague!

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:53.790
What?

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.630
It must have fallen from there during that last earthquake.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.050
The poor thing.

00:17:03.430 --> 00:17:05.940
I wonder if there's any way to get it back up.

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:07.590
Get it back up?

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.640
Hey, this is no time to be worrying about a Pague.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.480
At this rate, we'll...

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.650
Anyways, I'm going to take a look.

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:19.180
Howard and Sharla haven't come back?

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:22.060
It's been raining terribly for a while.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.500
That might be why they're not back, but...

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.000
Maybe something happened.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:27.390
Luna...

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:32.040
Let's all go together to look for them.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.450
This is terrible.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.550
She must have hurt it when she fell.

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:45.010
It looks like it'll be impossible to move her.

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.180
Well, let's go!

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:47.300
Wait a moment!

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:49.550
What are you doing?

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:51.240
Looking for herbs.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:52.630
Herbs?

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:54.760
Sharla, give it a break!

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:57.760
I don't care how much you want to go, I can't leave her alone!

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:01.230
If you want to go that badly, go ahead. I'll catch up with you later.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:05.380
Do whatever you want!

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:14.110
I figure they probably fell from here.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.610
I see, Kaoru, you too?

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.640
It looks that way, but it's hard to be sure.

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:19.630
How about it, Bell?

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.310
It's no use, I can't spot them!

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:24.390
Anyways, let's split up and search for them.

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:31.290
Let's take the boat to the bottom and look there.

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:40.290
Sharla! Howard! If you can hear me, answer!

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:45.540
They there?

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:47.540
They don't seem to be.

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:49.140
Let's go a little further.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:52.330
Tako!

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.880
What would we do if you fell?

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:07.630
You'll be fine now. The pain should go away soon.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.530
Stop that! It tickles!

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:13.030
Are you done?

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.790
Then let's get going.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:19.260
Howard, is there some way for us to get this Pague back to her child?

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:27.280
Howard!

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.710
Howard! Howard!

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:39.760
Howard!

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:44.560
Hurry up and give me your hand!

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.780
Hang on! I'll save you!

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:50.230
Grab on!

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:52.740
Howard!

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:54.310
Hang on tight, Howard!

00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:55.100
Just a little further!

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:56.110
Hang on!

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:57.950
Everyone!

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:01.780
Howard!

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.060
Are you okay?

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:05.710
Of course not!

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:08.560
--Keep it up!
--A little further!
--Stretch your arm out!

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.560
It's impossible! I can't reach that far!

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:12.390
Howard...

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:15.280
What's impossible is impossible!

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:17.860
Pague...

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:19.290
Pague!

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:20.300
Hang on!

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:21.580
Pague...

00:20:22.210 --> 00:20:23.300
You...

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:25.930
That's..

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:27.200
Howard 'n Sharla!

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:29.190
I'm saved!

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:30.990
Are you okay?

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:34.700
<i>Now</i> they get here.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.030
Pague!

00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:42.200
Luna!

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:44.040
We can make it!

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:44.680
I'll try!

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:56.600
Everyone!

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.130
Luna... Everyone...

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:20.340
They did it!

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:21.340
What a relief.

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:22.550
Everyone!

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:25.700
Next time tell us a little sooner when you're gonna do that.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:41.190
Take care!

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:44.120
Goodbye!

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.000
The wind has picked up.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:54.610
It feels good.

00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:56.380
It's always nice after the rain.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:59.300
As though everything has become clear.

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:04.930
You're right! You don't get this refreshin' feelin' in the colony.

00:22:04.930 --> 00:22:06.350
This is nature.

00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:21.500
I've decided.

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:24.390
I'm going to protect this planet!

00:22:25.030 --> 00:22:27.690
Whatever anyone else says, I'll protect it!

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:28.850
Howard!

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:32.190
I don't want to be seen as ungrateful, after all.

00:22:34.060 --> 00:22:36.500
It seems like there's no objections, then.

00:22:36.650 --> 00:22:37.590
Menori...

00:22:37.850 --> 00:22:38.380
Yes.

00:22:39.280 --> 00:22:41.260
Looks like we all came to the same conclusion.

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:43.330
Conclusion, conclusion!

00:22:45.650 --> 00:22:47.040
Alright, let's do it!

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:49.810
We'll blow away that gravity storm with our own hands!

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:08.340
The time has come for the space ship we're on to blast off and head for the gravity storm.

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:14.260
It's true we're scared, but it's thanks to this planet that we've been able to live like this.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:17.410
So we want to protect it. We have to protect it!

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:22.290
And no matter what happens, let's live through it and come back to this planet alive, everyone!

00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:28.210
Next time: Not going so we can die.
